\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.4}{\ignorespaces PIC simulations of reconnection from \cite  {Le_Egedal_Ohia_Daughton_Karimabadi_Lukin_2013}. The top row shows a moderate guide field run and the bottom row a low guide field run. With sufficiently high field, the pressure anisotropy in panel (a) stays in the outflow as compared to the low guide field. This leads to a marginal firehose condition of order $0.5$ (panel (b)) in the outflow which supports sharply bent field lines and a current jet in the center of the outflow (panel (c)).}}{10}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
